perturbations.a:
How can I obtain the raw command line arguments in a node.js application, given this example command:

node forwardwithssh.js echo "hello arguments"

process.argv will be [ "node", "/path/to/forwardwith.js", "echo", "hello arguments" ]

And there's no method to reconstruct the original echo "hello arguments" from that (ie. join(" " won't restore quotes back). I want the entire original raw string after the script name.

what I wish is easily acquired in bash scripts with "$*" , is there any corresponding way to obtain that in node.js?

Note: the purpose in particular is to receive a command to be executed elsewhere (eg. thru ssh)

Wrap each of the args in single quotes, and escape and single quotes within each arg to '\'' :

var cmd_string = process.argv.map( function(arg){
  return "'" + arg.replace(/'/g, "'\\''") + "'";
}).join(' ');

That would give you a cmd_string containing:

'node' '/path/to/forwardwith.js' 'echo' 'hello arguments'

which can be executed directly in another shell.

