perturbations.a:
I am employing a plugin for flutter called search_widget .  
The data argument of this widget accepts a list. But as I employ sqlite for retrieving data, I have it in Future shape.  
Is there any method I can transform Future to List ?  
Or any additional way to get this functioning.  

Borrowing the example from search_widget you need dataList in a widget like this:  

SearchWidget  
(  
   dataList: list,  
   textFieldBuilder: (TextEditingController controller, FocusNode focusNode) {  
     return MyTextField(controller, focusNode);  
   },  
 )  

Sure, you can transform Future into List like other responses indicate. But you won't be able to do dataList: await _sqliteCall(); because build methods are intended to be pure and sychronous.  

While the Future finishes you will have to return something like a progress indicator. For that you can utilize a FutureBuilder :  

FutureBuilder  
>(  
  future: _sqliteCall(),  
  builder: (context, snapshot) {  
    if (snapshot.hasData) {  
      return SearchWidget  
(  
        dataList: snapshot.data,  
        textFieldBuilder: (TextEditingController controller, FocusNode focusNode) {  
          return MyTextField(controller, focusNode);  
        },  
      )  
    }  
    return CircularProgressIndicator();  
  }  
),  

Of course this can also be accomplished with a StatefulWidget , you can check this article for a thorough explanation of the matter .

